---
// Follow one records request (part of #1440): what happens after you ask a
// West Virginia public body for a public record, on /public-records/. Uses
// the shared StepJourney shell. Every step comes from the state Freedom of
// Information Act as quoted in content/resources/wv-foia-request.yaml
// (W. Va. Code 29B-1-3 and 29B-1-5, read again 2026-11-14). No new facts.
// The drawing: a request moves from you, to the office, to its answer, and
// in the last step to the circuit court. In step 2 a strip of days fills in:
// five days, with a Saturday and Sunday that do not count. The strip is an
// example: the law does not say which weekday a request arrives, and the
// drawing does not say which day the count starts.
import StepJourney from './StepJourney.astro';
// Stations on the top row and where the request marker stands in each step.
const ST = { you: 40, office: 130, answer: 220, court: 290 };
const AT = [ST.you, ST.office, ST.answer, ST.answer, ST.court];
// The day strip: seven boxes, the third and fourth are the weekend.
const CELLS = ['1', '2', 'Sat', 'Sun', '3', '4', '5'];
const CX = 24, CW = 38, CG = 1;
const CHIPS = [['Copies', 'c1'], ['A time to look', 'c2'], ['A written no', 'c3']];
const scene = (s) => `<svg class="jr-scene rq-scene" data-s="${s}" viewBox="0 0 320 156" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <g class="e e-l1"><text class="tc" x="24" y="14">You send a written request.</text><text class="tx" x="24" y="28">To the office that keeps the record.</text></g>
  <g class="e e-l2"><text class="tc" x="24" y="14">The office has five days to answer.</text><text class="tx" x="24" y="28">Saturdays, Sundays and holidays don't count.</text></g>
  <g class="e e-l3"><text class="tc" x="24" y="14">It must do one of three things.</text><text class="tx" x="24" y="28">Send copies, set a time, or say no in writing.</text></g>
  <g class="e e-l4"><text class="tc" x="24" y="14">Copies: the cost of making them.</text><text class="tx" x="24" y="28">No fee for searching or pulling records.</text></g>
  <g class="e e-l5"><text class="tc" x="24" y="14">If it says no, you can go to court.</text><text class="tx" x="24" y="28">The circuit court where the record is kept.</text></g>
  <path class="track" d="M${ST.you} 52H${ST.answer}"/>
  <path class="track e e-court" d="M${ST.answer} 52H${ST.court}"/>
  ${Object.entries(ST).map(([k, x]) => `<g class="stn stn-${k}"><circle cx="${x}" cy="52" r="6"/><text class="tx" x="${x}" y="74" text-anchor="middle">${{ you: 'You', office: 'Office', answer: 'Answer', court: 'Court' }[k]}</text></g>`).join('')}
  <g class="mark"><rect x="${ST.you - 9}" y="40" width="18" height="12" rx="1"/><path d="M${ST.you - 9} 40l9 7l9 -7"/></g>
  <g class="e e-days">
    ${CELLS.map((t, i) => {
      const x = CX + i * (CW + CG);
      const wk = t === 'Sat' || t === 'Sun';
      return `<rect class="${wk ? 'cell wk' : 'cell'}" x="${x}" y="88" width="${CW}" height="26" rx="1"/>${wk ? '' : `<rect class="cell-on d${t}" x="${x}" y="88" width="${CW}" height="26" rx="1"/>`}<text class="${wk ? 'tx' : 'cn'}" x="${x + CW / 2}" y="105" text-anchor="middle">${t}</text>`;
    }).join('')}
    <text class="tx" x="24" y="132">Five days, not counting the weekend.</text>
    <text class="tx" x="24" y="146">A legal holiday also does not count.</text>
  </g>
  <g class="e e-chips">
    ${CHIPS.map(([t, c], i) => `<g class="chip ${c}"><rect x="${24 + i * 92}" y="88" width="88" height="26" rx="1"/><text x="${24 + i * 92 + 44}" y="105" text-anchor="middle">${t}</text></g>`).join('')}
    <text class="tx" x="24" y="132">Example drawing. The law gives these three</text>
    <text class="tx" x="24" y="146">answers; the office picks one.</text>
  </g>
  <path class="e e-up up" d="M${24 + 2 * 92 + 70} 86V64l${ST.court - (24 + 2 * 92 + 70)} -6"/>
</svg>`;
const steps = [
  {
    when: 'The day you ask', title: 'You send a written request', short: 'You send a request',
    body: [
      'Send it to the office that keeps the record. State law says a request "shall be made directly to the custodian of such public record" and "must state with reasonable specificity the information sought."',
      'Say exactly what you want, like the type of record, the dates, and the names or addresses involved. Keep a copy.',
    ],
  },
  {
    when: 'Up to five days', title: 'The office has five days to answer', short: 'Five days to answer',
    body: ['The law says the office must answer "as soon as is practicable but within a maximum of five days not including Saturdays, Sundays or legal holidays."'],
  },
  {
    when: 'The answer', title: 'One of three answers', short: 'One of three answers',
    body: ['The office must do one of three things: send copies, tell you the time and place you can look at and copy the records, or say no in writing and give the reasons.'],
  },
  {
    when: 'If you get copies', title: 'What copies can cost', short: 'What copies can cost',
    body: ['The law lets an office charge fees "reasonably calculated to reimburse it for its actual cost in making reproductions of records." It "may not charge a search or retrieval fee."'],
  },
  {
    when: 'If the answer is no', title: 'You can ask a court', short: 'You can ask a court',
    body: ['The law lets you ask the circuit court "in the county where the public record is kept" to look at it. The court can order the office to release records "improperly withheld."'],
  },
];
---
<StepJourney id="rq-explainer" heading="What happens after you ask" level={2} steps={steps} scene={scene} listLabel="One records request, step by step">
  <p>What happens after you ask for a public record, in the order state law sets out.</p>
  <Fragment slot="key"><strong>About the drawing:</strong> the steps are from West Virginia's Freedom of Information Act (<a href="https://code.wvlegislature.gov/29B-1-3/">W. Va. Code 29B-1-3</a> and <a href="https://code.wvlegislature.gov/29B-1-5/">29B-1-5</a>, checked November 14, 2026). The strip of days is an example week. It shows that weekends do not count, not which day the count starts.</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="summary">
    <p>Send a written request to the office that keeps the record. Within five days, not counting Saturdays, Sundays or legal holidays, it must send copies, set a time for you to look, or say no in writing with reasons. Copies can cost what they cost to make, with no search fee. If the answer is no, you can ask the circuit court in the county where the record is kept.</p>
    <p>This describes the law; it is not legal advice. Free and low cost legal help: <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/legal-help/`}>courts and legal help</a>.</p>
  </Fragment>
</StepJourney>

<style is:global>
  /* ===== Follow one records request. Press tokens only; scoped to #rq-explainer. ===== */
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .track { stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 4; fill: none; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .stn circle { fill: var(--card); stroke: var(--fg); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .mark rect { fill: var(--card); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2.5; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .mark path { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .cell { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .cell.wk { fill: var(--line); }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .cell-on { fill: var(--accent); opacity: 0; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .cn { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--fg); }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .chip rect { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--fg); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .chip text { font-weight: 700; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .up { fill: none; stroke: var(--rust); stroke-width: 2; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }

  /* What each step shows: one caption, the marker's place, the days or the answers. */
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="1"] .e-l1,
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="2"] .e-l2,
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="3"] .e-l3,
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="4"] .e-l4,
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="5"] .e-l5,
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene:is([data-s="1"], [data-s="2"]) .e-days,
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene:is([data-s="3"], [data-s="4"], [data-s="5"]) .e-chips,
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="5"] :is(.e-court, .e-up) { opacity: 1; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene .stn-court { opacity: 0.35; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="5"] .stn-court { opacity: 1; }
  /* In step 2 the five counted days fill in; the weekend stays gray. */
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="2"] .cell-on { opacity: 0.35; }
  /* Step 4 points at copies, step 5 at the written no. */
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="4"] .chip:not(.c1),
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="5"] .chip:not(.c3) { opacity: 0.35; }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="2"] .mark { transform: translateX(90px); }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="3"] .mark,
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="4"] .mark { transform: translateX(180px); }
  #rq-explainer .rq-scene[data-s="5"] .mark { transform: translateX(250px); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    #rq-explainer.is-live .jr-stage .cell-on.d2 { transition-delay: 0.15s; }
    #rq-explainer.is-live .jr-stage .cell-on.d3 { transition-delay: 0.3s; }
    #rq-explainer.is-live .jr-stage .cell-on.d4 { transition-delay: 0.45s; }
    #rq-explainer.is-live .jr-stage .cell-on.d5 { transition-delay: 0.6s; }
  }
</style>
